# Adoption marker for SDDK Framework

> **This file marks the project as adopted.** `sddk-init` checks for this file in O(1) to skip the heavy adoption check on every subsequent run.
>
> Do NOT delete this file. If you delete it, future `sddk-init` invocations will warn about missing adoption.

## What this means

- `.sddk-knowledge/` exists and is committed to git
- `.gitignore` blocks SDDK working artifacts from accidental commits
- `.ignore` makes them readable by ripgrep/agents
- `openspec/config.yaml` is configured for this project
- `.atl/skill-registry.md` indexes available skills
- Legacy ADRs (if any) are migrated to the vault as `LEGACY-*.md` nodes

## How to start a cycle

```bash
cd {project}
# /sddk-init will detect .adopted marker and skip the heavy check (O(1))
/sddk-new <change-name>
```

## How to undo adoption (rare)

```bash
rm .sddk-knowledge/.adopted
# Future sddk-init will warn about missing adoption
```
